WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.110
December 24th, 1986 (Wednesday)

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.110
December 24th, 1986 (Wednesday)

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.530
nemuri nasai ima wa tada

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.530
Sleep, for now

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:15.440
watashi no naka de doko ni mo ikanai de

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:15.440
Inside of me, and don't go anywhere

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:36.450
madoromi no fuchi de yureteru gunjou iro no yo

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:36.450
Through the slumbering ultramarine sky

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:41.970
majiwaru koto no nai hoshi wo sagashiteru

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:41.970
I am searching for stars that will never cross

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:49.670
anata wo motomeru yubisaki yami ni samayotte

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:49.670
These fingertips search for you, but are lost in darkness

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:58.550
mogaite mo nukedesenai ai no umi ni oboreteku

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:58.550
I try but I can't escape, and I drown in the sea of love

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:06.440
yawaranai toiki ni kokoro sae mo furueru

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:06.440
Your tender sigh makes my heart tremble

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:12.060
karamaru utsukushi kumo no ito no you

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:12.060
Seemingly entangled in the beautiful strands of a spider web

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.550
ugokenai no watashi wo yurushite

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.550
I cannot move, please forgive me

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:19.880
anata no ude ni dakarete nemuru

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:19.880
I am sleeping with your arms around me

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.100
nani mo kamo sutetatte ii

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.100
I don't mind losing anything else

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:30.630
ii kono mama no maboroshi nante zukuru no wa yamete

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:30.630
Stop pretending that you are a good girl

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.090
hontou no watashi wo mitsukete

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.090
Find the real me

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:40.170
zutto matteru

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:40.170
I'll be waiting forever

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.660
<b>Hey, what are you doing?</b>

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.170
<b>Haruka-chi!</b>

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.130
<b>What's wrong with everyone? Did someone die?</b>

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.830
<b>Nobody died.</b>

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.970
<b>That's not something you should be saying here.</b>

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.220
<b>Sorry.</b>

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.380
<b>Who are you?</b>

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.110
<b>I'm a Zashiki Warashi.</b>

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:24.830
Page 14
I've never been able to tune properly.
I can't help but think I could be better.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.740
<b>What? Are they taking advantage of us?</b>

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.020
<b>Then we have no choice.</b>

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.610
<b>Ineda, go and deposit one billion yen.</b>

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:52.620
Christmas Eve Miracle! Rina is unstoppable! - Out of nowhere, Ogata Rina, the idol queen!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.500
The miracle of Christmas, Morikawa Yuki also fights bravely! - Considering the turnout, she can no longer be simply called a novice!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:03.430
Sakura-dan falls! Conspicuous empty seats, with people also leaving during the show... - Booed at when they forgot their lyrics

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.590
The Ogata combo completely victorious! - Idol Queen Ogata Rina & Morikawa Yuki sing passionately!

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.800
<b>Yuki, you came...</b>

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.490
<b>My manager contacted me.</b>

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.550
<b>Ah.</b>

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:34.050
<b>Fujii-kun went back to get his father's belongings.</b>

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.660
<b>How is Touya's dad?</b>

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.130
<b>His heart is...</b>

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.890
<b>It seems like it was bad for a while now.</b>

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.880
<b>Fujii-kun didn't seem to know about it.</b>

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.280
<b>His heart?</b>

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.010
<b>So, it wasn't a case of hemorrhoids?</b>

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:58.530
<b>Is that what Fujii-kun told you it was?</b>

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.970
<b>Yuki...</b>

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.290
<b>Oh, Yuki...</b>

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.000
<b>There's no need to worry.</b>

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.200
<b>He'll have surgery early in the new year.</b>

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.640
<b>He'll be fine, he's still young.</b>

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.140
<b>The doctors said he'll definitely recover.</b>

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.100
<b>The one who has it worst is Fujii-kun.</b>

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:50.360
<b>Are you family members?</b>

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.440
<b>Ah, n-</b>

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:52.320
<b>We are.</b>

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.750
<b>He woke up just now.</b>

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.920
<b>You're?</b>

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.360
<b>I'm Morikawa Yuki.</b>

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.380
<b>You haven't changed.</b>

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.210
<b>Ah, I mean...</b>

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.090
<b>You've become very beautiful.</b>

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.000
<b>I'm sorry for having to meet you in this condition.</b>

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.550
<b>Where's my idiot of a son?</b>

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.650
<b>He went back home...</b>

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.190
<b>I'll tell him you visited.</b>

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:37.950
<b>It doesn't look like you have much time.</b>

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.040
<b>I...</b>

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.380
<b>I'm fine.</b>

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:49.060
<b>I like Touya-kun the way he is now.</b>

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.810
<b>Don't-</b>

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.470
<b>Yuki, your manager...</b>

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:17.080
<b>Why did you let her leave?!</b>

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:25.330
<b>You knew I was coming back. You could've tried a little harder to stop her.</b>

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.660
<b>But I suppose you're inconsiderate like that.</b>

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:31.940
<b>She seemed busy, unlike you.</b>

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:34.720
<b>I asked her to leave promptly.</b>

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.150
<b>And plus, Yuki-san-</b>

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:40.850
<b>Morikawa-san didn't come to see you.</b>

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.020
<b>She came to visit me.</b>

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:46.460
<b>It's obvious that visiting you was just an excuse!</b>

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:50.710
<b>Jeez, you collapsed and had to be brought to the hospital, and you're still trying to flirt?!</b>

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.380
<b>You-</b>

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.590
<b>Tell me. Where do you think we are?</b>

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:03.410
<b>Do you know why your father was hospitalized?</b>

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:06.290
<b>I'm going home.</b>

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:07.560
<b>Misaki-san!</b>

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.530
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.370
<b>Keep that mouth shut for the rest of your life.</b>

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.570
<b>Here she is!</b>

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.740
<b>Where was she?</b>

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.210
<b>Why?</b>

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.100
<b>It seems like she was waiting in front of the door after the concert.</b>

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.280
<b>And...</b>

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.920
<b>Why didn't you contact us?</b>

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.400
<b>Please don't yell at her.</b>

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.070
<b>What's the meaning of this?</b>

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.040
<b>It seems like she was told not to say anything.</b>

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.540
<b>But still...</b>

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:26.960
<b>Her room was occupied, so she stayed at a late-night cafe.</b>

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.610
<b>What are you doing?!</b>

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:53.530
<b>Ah.</b>

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:55.200
<b>Don't you "ah" me!</b>

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.100
<b>Get up!</b>

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.180
<b>You, you little...</b>

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:05.580
<b>I had nowhere to go, since they were keeping guard in front of my apartment.</b>

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.510
<b>Why didn't you show up? Why didn't you go?!</b>

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.990
<b>Oh, you're talking about the concert?</b>

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:13.240
<b>It went on fine without me, right?</b>

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:14.540
<b>Since I'm-</b>

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:25.070
<b>Think about the girls who had to sing the same song three times!</b>

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:29.850
<b>Do you have any idea how much loss you've incurred?!</b>

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.340
<b>You idiot!</b>

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:38.480
<b>Idiot!</b>

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:39.780
<b>Please stop.</b>

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.130
<b>There's nothing to gain and everything to lose from breaking her.</b>

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:45.650
<b>If she breaks, we'll just fix her by force!</b>

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:47.390
<b>Please calm down.</b>

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.250
<b>This is no time to be having an argument.</b>

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:52.700
<b>The Sakura-dan lost.</b>

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.790
<b><i>We</i> lost.</b>

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.260
<b>I know that.</b>

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.700
<b>Someone had to lose the match.</b>

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.740
<b>That's not what I meant.</b>

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:06.110
<b>You do understand, right?</b>

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:10.550
<b>The talents of Ogata Rina, and the potential of Morikawa Yuki.</b>

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:13.380
<b>We simply don't have the firepower...</b>

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:16.510
<b>... to stand against them.</b>

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:20.410
<b>Hmph. Fans nowadays are fed up with trained professionals.</b>

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:23.190
<b>From now on, it's the age of amateurs.</b>

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:25.300
<b>Just look at how things turned out.</b>

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:27.620
<b>Please don't take it the wrong way.</b>

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.750
<b>What?</b>

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.850
<b>Aren't you the great Kanzaki Itsuki?</b>

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:37.820
<b>No one said anything about taking care of these girls so that they have a bright future.</b>

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.420
<b>I think I told you this before.</b>

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.920
<b>Two songs per girl is the maximum.</b>

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:46.390
<b>Before the fans start to feel dissatisfied, we pull them out and find replacements-</b>

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:48.920
<b>You're talking as if replacing the girls doesn't cost anything.</b>

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.720
<b>Do you have any idea how much money I spent on the Sakura-dan?</b>

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.630
<b>If we don't do something about this idiot, we're d-</b>

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:56.650
<b>Like I said!</b>

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:58.670
<b>We'll figure something out.</b>

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:02.400
<b>President Ogata will see all this if we don't go back soon.</b>

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:05.550
<b>Let's go.</b>

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.340
<b>Uh, umm...</b>

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.770
<b>What should we do with Menou-san?</b>

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.400
<b>Don't let her go back into her apartment.</b>

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.680
<b>Throw her into a storehouse until she realizes her mistakes.</b>

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.670
<b>Hey, do you want to go to the beach?</b>

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.620
<b>You'll catch a cold.</b>

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.350
<b>Nii-san.</b>

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.810
<b>Did I lose?</b>

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:54.620
<b>Or did I-</b>

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.080
<b>Eh? To Yuki?</b>

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.220
<b>That's not...</b>

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:03.340
<b>... what I was talking about!</b>

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.740
<b>Ah, that's of no concern to me.</b>

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:06.770
<b>It's already over.</b>

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:09.020
<b>I'm sorry!</b>

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:09.460
<b>You're late.</b>

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.390
<b>My apologies. We were caught in traffic.</b>

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:11.940
<b>Nii-san!</b>

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.150
<b>We're short of time. That can wait.</b>

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.830
<b>It's important.</b>

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.390
<b>This is more important.</b>

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:17.260
<b>More important...</b>

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:18.800
<b>... than me?</b>

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:19.750
<b>Yes.</b>

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.230
<b>It's time to exploit our victory.</b>

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:35.690
Mobilization value - Ogata Productions

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:30.580
<b>I want to talk about our plan from now on.</b>

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:35.660
<b>Judging from the attendance of last night's concert, I have reason to believe Yuki has the potential I saw in her.</b>

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:38.670
<b>It's good that you've improved as well, Rina.</b>

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:42.620
<b>With Rina and Yuki with Ogata Productions, we'll be in a very favorable position next year.</b>

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:43.980
<b>That's all.</b>

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:47.270
<b>President.</b>

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.680
<b>What about today's lesson?</b>

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:50.860
<b>You have the day off today.</b>

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.360
<b>Merry Christmas, Yuki.</b>

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.060
<b>Rina-chan, you had something important to tell your brother?</b>

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.880
<b>N-Not really.</b>

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.940
<b>Aren't you busy?</b>

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:09.240
<b>I probably won't see my brother until next year.</b>

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:13.730
<b>If you want, I can pass your message on to him tomorrow.</b>

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.290
<b>Don't worry about it.</b>

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.830
<b>You'd rather tell him yourself. I see.</b>

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.850
<b>That's not it.</b>

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.950
<b>I've already missed my chance to tell him.</b>

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:29.340
<b>How is it?</b>

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.350
<b>It's wonderful.</b>

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:36.280
<b>I don't think it's beautiful enough to warrant your staring at it for so long.</b>

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:39.350
<b>Is it because of this country's atmosphere?</b>

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:41.310
<b>It's different from when I saw it back in London...</b>

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:45.330
<b>It must look different to you now, since it's now yours.</b>

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.760
<b>Hurry up and take it.</b>

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:52.590
<b>This is the first time you've admitted defeat, isn't it?</b>

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.600
<b>You just got lucky last night.</b>

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:56.900
<b>It all starts now.</b>

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:05.400
<b>Spoon...</b>

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.550
<b>Spoon, spoon... there are no spoons.</b>

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.400
<b>A ladle.</b>

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.400
<b>Where's the ladle...</b>

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.940
<b>Gosh, where is her mom and what is she doing?</b>

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.160
<b>Who are you?</b>

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:25.700
<b>If she would've just eaten everything she was given, she wouldn't have caught a cold.</b>

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.170
<b>Her entrance exams are coming up, too...</b>

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.930
<b>I'm glad she has friends like you.</b>

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.340
<b>Fujii-sensei must also be a great person, right?</b>

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:52.340
<b>All right, full speed ahead!</b>

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.270
<b>Haruka-chi!</b>

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:15.000
<b>Haruka-chi!</b>

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.370
<b>Why did you come?</b>

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.900
<b>You should be in bed!</b>

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.700
<b>How's your fever?</b>

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:26.850
<b>Thanks to your porridge, it's all gone!</b>

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.090
<b>And your mom?</b>

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.030
<b>She went out right after you left.</b>

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.300
<b>She probably won't come back tonight.</b>

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:36.910
<b>So, I can bike with you for a little bit, right?</b>

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.070
<b>Come on...</b>

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:41.820
<b>It's Christmas.</b>

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:53.130
ai to iu katachi nai mono torawareteiru

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:53.130
I'm trapped by something that lacks the shape of love.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:17:01.020
shinzou ga tomaru you na koi ga aru koto shitteru

00:16:54.050 --> 00:17:01.020
But I know there's such a thing as a love that stops your heart.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:09.540
au tabi no ataetekureta akogare de sae

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:09.540
The respect that I have for you, each time we meet...

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:16.640
ima demo shinjiteiru mou kieru koto wa nai

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:16.640
If I believe in that, it'll never go away.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:24.420
raku wo sezu tsukiru koto no nai jounetsu wa

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:24.420
This practically inexhaustible passion of mine...

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:32.800
doko kara kuru no dokoka ni nemutteiru no kana

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:32.800
Where's it coming from? Where's it resting?

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.470
<b>And the next song is by Matsuyama Menou-</b>

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:40.700
lala hoshi ga ima unmei wo egaku yo musuu no hikari kagayaku

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:40.700
La la, the stars point out our destinies out of limitless, dazzling light.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:48.430
ima hitotsu dake kimeta koto ga aru anata to wa hanarenai

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:48.430
The one thing I've decided on my own is that I'll never leave you.

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:45.890
